  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-image-preview",
      "text": "English | [简体中文](README.zh.md)\n\nInline image previews for the built-in DeepSeek Harness `read_image` tool.\n\nThe plugin uses DSH's public, session-scoped `tool.call.toolview` slot. Because the official tool tree dispatches nested subcalls through the same slot, one renderer covers both:\n\n- direct `read_image` calls; and\n- `tools.read_image(...)` calls nested inside `run_code` Code Mode."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-image-preview",
      "text": "Every loaded preview includes **Copy image** with visible success or failure feedback. PNG bytes are copied directly when supported; other accepted formats are converted to PNG in-browser when necessary."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security and lifecycle",
      "text": "- Bytes are fetched only through `ctx.sessions.binding(sessionId).session.readAttachment(attachmentId)`.\n- The model-supplied file path is display/navigation metadata only and is never reread by the browser plugin.\n- Only authenticated PNG, JPEG, WebP, and GIF attachment responses are rendered.\n- Blob URLs are revoked on replacement, retry, unmount, and HMR disposal.\n- Clipboard copies use the same authenticated attachment blob; bounded in-browser conversion never rereads the model-supplied path or adds a network fallback.\n- Malformed/legacy results and attachment RPC failures degrade to a bounded inline error with no filesystem or network fallback."
    },
    {
      "section": "Settings",
      "text": "The plugin contributes an **Image previews** card under DSH Settings → Plugins with two live, persisted options:\n\n- **Enable inline previews** — disabling it removes the custom renderer and restores DSH's generic tool row.\n- **Open previews automatically** — when disabled, each image starts collapsed and loads only after **Show preview** is clicked."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "Requires DeepSeek Harness 0.1.2-alpha.2 or compatible.\n\n```sh\npnpm install\npnpm check\n```\n\nThe package follows the official [Harness plugin guide](https://deepseek-harness.github.io/deepseek-harness/en/develop/basic/): it exports a function-form host plugin, declares a `dsh.bundle` patch, exposes a Web client entry, declares its injected public packages, and owns explicit cleanup through lifecycle effects."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install into a profile",
      "text": "A tarball avoids git-build permissions and is robust when the checkout path contains spaces:\n\n```sh\npnpm pack --pack-destination \"$HOME/.dsh/packages\"\ndsh plugin --profile web add \"$HOME/.dsh/packages/dsh-image-preview-0.3.4.tgz\"\ndsh --profile web --dump-config\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install into a profile",
      "text": "The install command adds the package dependency and appends `dsh-image-preview` to the profile's ordered bundle list. Refresh the page after the running Web profile has loaded the new bundle; a first-time host mount requires an operator-approved Web restart."
    }
  ],
